*Heading
** Edgebreakout set-up (drawings sheets 3-6): half model, symmetry plane z = 0, c = 150
** Mesh: mesh/generate_edgebreakout_setup.py (Cubit) + mesh/modifyMesh.py.  Units: mm, N, MPa, tonne.
** x = pull direction (towards the free edge), y = vertical (concrete top at y = 0), z = across.
*Preprint, echo=NO, model=NO, history=NO, contact=NO
**
** UEL
**
*Include, input="./incfiles/ueldef.inc"
**
** PARTS
**
*Part, name=concrete
*Include, input="./mesh/modified/concrete.inp"
*Solid Section, elset=dummy, material=dummy
*End Part
**
** steel part = anchor, mortar, sleeve, washer, nut, C-section, L-beam, support plate, timber
*Part, name=steel
*Include, input="./mesh/modified/steel.inp"
*Solid Section, elset=ANCHOR, material=STEEL_ANCHOR
*Solid Section, elset=SLEEVE, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=WASHER, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=NUT, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=CSECTION, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=LBEAM, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=PLATE, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=HPLATE, material=STEEL_PLATE
*Solid Section, elset=TIMBER, material=TIMBER
*ORIENTATION, name=MORTAR_CYL, SYSTEM=CYLINDRICAL
0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0
1
**
** Cohesive Section (mortar)
*COHESIVE SECTION, elset=MORTAR, material=stick_slip, response=TRACTION SEPARATION, ORIENTATION=MORTAR_CYL, STACK DIRECTION=ORIENTATION
*End Part
**
** UEL Props
**
*Include, input="./incfiles/uelprops_GCDP.inc"
**
** ASSEMBLY
**
*Assembly, name=Assembly
**
*Instance, name=concrete-1, part=concrete
*End Instance
**
*Instance, name=steel-1, part=steel
*End Instance
**
** ---- TIED INTERFACES ----
** bonded anchor: anchor - mortar - concrete (as in the SS-160 model)
*TIE, NAME=ANCHOR_TO_MORTAR, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.mortar_to_anchor, steel-1.anchor_to_mortar
*TIE, NAME=MORTAR_TO_CONCRETE, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
concrete-1.concrete_to_mortar, steel-1.mortar_to_concrete
** steel sleeve (height 20, bore = anchor) is tied to the anchor
*TIE, NAME=SLEEVE_TO_ANCHOR, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.sleeve_bore, steel-1.anchor_to_mortar
** washer clamps the C web and the sleeve; nut clamps the washer (fixture fully tied, accuracy not critical)
*TIE, NAME=WASHER_TO_SLEEVE, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.washer_bottom, steel-1.sleeve_top
*TIE, NAME=WASHER_TO_WEB, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.washer_bottom, steel-1.c_webtop
*TIE, NAME=NUT_TO_WASHER, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.nut_bottom, steel-1.washer_top
*TIE, NAME=NUT_TO_ANCHOR, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.nut_bore, steel-1.anchor_to_mortar
** L-beam web bolted to the C flange: the M14 bolts are replaced by a tie of the contact faces
*TIE, NAME=LWEB_TO_CFLANGE, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE
steel-1.l_web_inner, steel-1.c_flange_outer
*End Assembly
